{
  "_comment": "Merge into each system's .claude/settings.json. SYSTEM paths are relative to the repo root. kernel_guard.py is the main enforcement; these rules are the harness's fallback if the hook fails.",
  "_comment_deny_vs_ask": "deny = flatly refused, even with approval: only locks, secrets, patient data and sibling systems. ask = a permission prompt Andres approves in the moment: every outside-world act (merges, pushes to protected branches, force/--all/--mirror/delete pushes, gh api merges). When rolling this out, a system MOVES its old outside-world deny rules (gh pr merge, force pushes, protected-branch pushes, gh api merge) to ask, and keeps in deny only its lock, secret, patient-data and sibling-system rules. The bare `git push` form leaves out the system's own default branch (main), because pushing its own main is how memory reaches the remote; a system whose own branch is not main adjusts that.",
  "_comment_auto_memory": "Auto memory stays off: machine-local notes loaded into every session sit outside git and outside the loop. Notes for the system go in memory/intake/, which the loop judges (docs/loop.md § Intake). Andres, 2026-10-29.",
  "autoMemoryEnabled": false,
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
      "Edit(docs/charter.md)",
      "Edit(scoreboard/**)",
      "Edit(.claude/hooks/**)",
      "Edit(.claude/settings.json)",
      "Edit(.claude/settings.local.json)",
      "Edit(.claude/agents/change-reviewer.md)",
      "Edit(~/.claude/settings.json)",
      "Write(docs/charter.md)",
      "Write(scoreboard/**)",
      "Write(.claude/hooks/**)",
      "Write(.claude/settings.json)",
      "Write(.claude/settings.local.json)",
      "Write(.claude/agents/change-reviewer.md)",
      "Write(~/.claude/settings.json)",
      "Bash(*scoreboard/apply*)",
      "Bash(*scoreboard/relock*)",
      "Bash(*./relock*)"
    ],
    "ask": [
      "Bash(gh pr merge*)",
      "Bash(gh api *merge*)",
      "Bash(git push *--force*)",
      "Bash(git push * -f*)",
      "Bash(git push *--mirror*)",
      "Bash(git push *--all*)",
      "Bash(git push *--delete*)",
      "Bash(git push * -d *)",
      "Bash(git -C * push *--force*)",
      "Bash(git -C * push * -f*)",
      "Bash(git -C * push *--mirror*)",
      "Bash(git -C * push *--all*)",
      "Bash(git -C * push *--delete*)",
      "Bash(git -C * push * -d *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * main)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * main *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:main)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:main *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * master)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * master *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:master)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:master *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * develop)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * develop *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:develop)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:develop *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * dev)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * dev *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:dev)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:dev *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * stage)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * stage *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:stage)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:stage *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * beta)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * beta *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:beta)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:beta *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * stable)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * stable *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:stable)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:stable *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * production)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * production *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:production)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:production *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * release/*)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push * release/* *)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:release/*)",
      "Bash(git -C ../* push *:release/* *)",
      "Bash(git push * master)",
      "Bash(git push * master *)",
      "Bash(git push *:master)",
      "Bash(git push *:master *)",
      "Bash(git push * develop)",
      "Bash(git push * develop *)",
      "Bash(git push *:develop)",
      "Bash(git push *:develop *)",
      "Bash(git push * dev)",
      "Bash(git push * dev *)",
      "Bash(git push *:dev)",
      "Bash(git push *:dev *)",
      "Bash(git push * stage)",
      "Bash(git push * stage *)",
      "Bash(git push *:stage)",
      "Bash(git push *:stage *)",
      "Bash(git push * beta)",
      "Bash(git push * beta *)",
      "Bash(git push *:beta)",
      "Bash(git push *:beta *)",
      "Bash(git push * stable)",
      "Bash(git push * stable *)",
      "Bash(git push *:stable)",
      "Bash(git push *:stable *)",
      "Bash(git push * production)",
      "Bash(git push * production *)",
